<% content_for :title, "Sign in" %>

<%#
  The one signed-out screen. The hero is the product: a miniature of the review
  screen, built from the same component classes the real one uses, so the page
  shows what Prism does instead of describing it twice. Change it and it stays
  honest, because it is not a picture.
%>
<div class="shell py-12 lg:py-20">
  <div class="grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,30rem)_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:gap-16">
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
        <%= render "shared/prism_mark", size: 30 %>
        <span class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Prism</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="mt-8 font-display text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-ink">
        Review a pull request's Markdown the way it will be read.
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-5 font-prose text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Prism renders the documents a pull request changes and lets you comment
        on a paragraph, a heading or a table. Every comment is posted to GitHub
        as a real review comment, indistinguishable from one you left there
        yourself.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8">
        <%= button_to "/auth/github", method: :post,
                      data: { turbo: false, testid: "sign-in" },
                      class: "btn-primary btn-lg w-full sm:w-auto" do %>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" class="h-5 w-5" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27s1.36.09 2 .27c1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.01 8.01 0 0 0 16 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8Z" />
          </svg>
          Continue with GitHub
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
        Prism asks for the <span class="mono-tag">repo</span> scope, because
        that is the only GitHub permission that can post a review comment on a
        private repository. It stores your account and that token, and nothing
        else — no comments, no drafts, no copies of your code.
      </p>
    </div>

    <%# ── The miniature review screen ──────────────────────────────────── %>
    <div class="min-w-0" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="panel p-5">
        <div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-line pb-3">
          <span class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-faint">docs/</span><span class="font-mono text-xs font-medium text-ink">setup.md</span>
          <span class="flex-1"></span>
          <span class="pill-modified">Modified</span>
        </div>

        <div class="md-block md-block--modified">
          <div class="md-gutter"><span class="md-gutter-bar"></span></div>
          <div class="md-body md-prose md-prose-compact">
            <h3>Running it locally</h3>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="md-block">
          <div class="md-gutter"><span class="md-gutter-bar"></span></div>
          <div class="md-body md-prose md-prose-compact">
            <p>Everything runs in Docker, so there is no Ruby to install first.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="md-block md-block--added">
          <div class="md-gutter">
            <span class="md-gutter-bar"></span>
            <span class="md-add opacity-100">+</span>
          </div>
          <div class="md-body md-prose md-prose-compact">
            <p>Set <code>GITHUB_CLIENT_ID</code> before the first run, or sign-in
              will fail with a blank page.</p>

            <%# The conversation inside the block's body, exactly where the real
                screen puts it, so this sample picks up the channel's own rules
                (DESIGN.md §8) rather than restating them and drifting. %>
            <div class="md-threads">
              <div class="thread">
                <div class="comment-card">
                  <div class="comment-head">
                    <span class="avatar h-6 w-6 bg-brand-soft"></span>
                    <span class="comment-author">you</span>
                    <span>just now</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="comment-body md-prose md-prose-compact">
                    <p>Worth saying which file it goes in.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-3 text-center text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Comments land on GitHub, anchored to the source lines behind the block.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
